    {
      "id": "CARD-AM-06-concept",
      "conceptId": "C-AM-06",
      "kind": "concept",
      "title": {
        "en": "Coherent demodulation and recovery gain",
        "or": "Coherent demodulation ଓ Recovery gain"
      },
      "body": {
        "en": "A coherent receiver multiplies the DSB-SC signal by a local oscillator matched to the transmitted carrier in frequency and phase. For unit-amplitude carriers, the product is m(t)*cos^2(2*pi*fc*t). Using cos^2(theta)=[1+cos(2*theta)]/2, this contains m(t)/2 plus a high-frequency term around twice the carrier. Lowpass filtering removes that high-frequency term while retaining the message band. A recovery gain of 2 restores the ideal message amplitude when both carrier amplitudes are one. A practical filter can still alter amplitude and phase slightly. Coherent recovery preserves message sign, whereas a simple envelope detector cannot recover a general signed DSB-SC message correctly.",
        "or": "Coherent receiver ର local oscillator କୁ transmitted Carrier ସହିତ Frequency ଓ Phase ରେ ମେଳାଇବାକୁ ପଡ଼େ। Unit-amplitude Carrier ପାଇଁ product m(t)*cos^2(2*pi*fc*t)। cos^2(theta)=[1+cos(2*theta)]/2 ରୁ m(t)/2 ଏବଂ ଉଚ୍ଚ Frequency ଅଂଶ ମିଳେ। Lowpass filter message band କୁ ରଖି ଉଚ୍ଚ Frequency ଅଂଶ କମାଏ। Carrier amplitude ଦୁଇଟି 1 ହେଲେ Gain 2 ideal message amplitude ଫେରାଏ। Practical filter କିଛି Amplitude ଓ Phase ପରିବର୍ତ୍ତନ କରିପାରେ। Coherent recovery message ର ଚିହ୍ନ ରଖେ; ସରଳ Envelope detector ସାଧାରଣ signed DSB-SC message ଠିକ ଭାବରେ ଫେରାଇପାରେ ନାହିଁ।"
      },
